body:
Hi! I have a documentation issue on InstantSearch.js, I could not find what I was looking for which is: 

I have built a custom widget using your guide. I am using a multiple select list using jquery. I am trying to refine the search results with multiple values but I am not sure how to feed the values back. Your documentation only shows how to feed a single variable. Here is a sample of what I am trying to do:

```js
const refine = renderParams.refine;
$(container).find('select').on('change', function(event) {
     //array of selected options
     var selectedOptions = $(container).find('select').val();
     //sending array to algolia
     refine(selectedOptions);
});
```

Thanks,
Joe

comments.body:
@JoeStark110 Thanks for the example. Very helpful!

The menu behavior only refine on a single value. The behavior of `refine` in this context is to remove the previously selected value and refine the new one.

If you want to select multiple value, you should use the [connectRefinementList](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/connectors/connectRefinementList.html). Its `refine` will also take one item at a time, but is cumulative. Also if you refine on a value that is already selected, it will unselect it.
